@725 = ~Static Shock~
@726 = ~Static Shock (Alteration)
Level: 2
Range: 0
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: radius 2.5 meters
Saving Throw: none

The static shock spell uses electricity naturally present in the air to hurt the opponents of the mage. When the warlord casts this spell, any static electricity around him focuses on the nearby creatures and electrocutes them, dealing 1D8 damage every 2 levels of the caster (maximum 5D8, saving throw to halve).~
@7261 = ~Static Shock (Alteration)
Level: 2
Range: 0
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: radius 2.5 meters
Saving Throw: none

The static shock spell uses electricity naturally present in the air to hurt the opponents of the mage. When the warlord casts this spell, any static electricity around him focuses on the nearby creatures and electrocutes them, dealing 5D8 points of damage (a saving throw to halve).~

@727 = ~Mirror Image~
@728 = ~Mirror Image (Illusion)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates several duplicates of the mage. The number of duplicates depends on caster level:
Level 3 to 5  : 1D4
Level 6 to 8  : 1D6
Level 9 to 11 : 1D4+2
Level 12 to 14: 1D6+2
Level 15 to 17: 1D4+4
Level 18+     : 1D6+4
These images do exactly what the wizard does. Since the spell causes a blurring and slight distortion when it is cast, it is impossible for opponents to be certain which are the illusions and which is the actual wizard. When an image is struck by a melee or missile attack, magical or otherwise, it disappears, but any other existing images remain intact until they are struck. However, it is important to note that this will not protect the caster against every attack as it is possible for an enemy to choose the real caster amongst all the images.~
@7281 = ~Mirror Image (Illusion)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates several duplicates of the mage. The number of copies that appear is random: 1D6 +4.
These images do exactly what the wizard does. Since the spell causes a blurring and slight distortion when it is cast, it is impossible for opponents to be certain which are the illusions and which is the actual wizard. When an image is struck by a melee or missile attack, magical or otherwise, it disappears, but any other existing images remain intact until they are struck. However, it is important to note that this will not protect the caster against every attack as it is possible for an enemy to choose the real caster amongst all the images.~
