Saving Throw: none

This spell creates several duplicates of the recipient. The number of copies that appear is random: 1D6 +4.
These images do exactly what the recipient does. Since the spell causes a blurring and slight distortion when it is cast, it is impossible for opponents to be certain which are the illusions and which is the actual recipient. When an image is struck by a melee or missile attack, magical or otherwise, it disappears, but any other existing images remain intact until they are struck. However, it is important to note that this will not protect the recipient against every attack as it is possible for an enemy to choose the real recipient amongst all the images.~
